{
  "dom_id": "step-q164411",
  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "The projection of the intersection between the hyperbolic cylinder $3(x+1)^{2}-6(z-2)^{2}=12$ and the plane $y=1$ onto the $xz$-plane is a hyperbola. What are the lengths of the semi-axes of the hyperbola?",
  "worked_solution": "To find the intersection of the cylinder and the plane $y=1,$ we substitute $y=1$ into the equation of the cylinder. However, since the equation has no (explicit) $y$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x+1)^{2}-6(z-2)^{2} & =12 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(z-2)^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{(2)^{2}}-\\frac{(z-2)^{2}}{(\\sqrt{2})^{2}} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a hyperbola with semi-axes of lengths $2$ and $\\sqrt{2}.$",
